<title>USA: RTZ's Kennecott, union continue talks.</title>
<headline>RTZ's Kennecott, union continue talks.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Officials of the United Steelworkers and Kennecott Utah Copper Corp met on Monday in further talks aimed at reaching a new work contract, the company and union said.</p>
<p>Kennecott workers went out on strike on Wednesday, but returned to their jobs two days later as negotiations continued.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for the company, a unit of London-based RTZ Corp Plc, said a new proposal was given to union leadership, but a union spokeswoman could only confirm that talks were held on Monday.</p>
<p>A three-year contract expired on September 30. Details on the fresh Kennecott proposal were not disclosed.</p>
</text>
